  "body": "App version: 5.0.5\nApp commit: 07d8082abaf9d1aabd3f91058ff1430d2097f0c4\nCore commit: 123602be34ab6fa9725bb93f0d3bc27a630c7b44\n\nJava receiver commit (contract checks): 60d97c783f29da767fafe503980812101f6aa61f\n\nAll installer targets, core/app tests, companion checks and Windows assistant tests passed in this workflow run.\nCompanion E2E uses a scripted provider over the real local relay. It does not validate a live Claude account.\nThe packaged sidecar passed fresh configuration, a LAN-address pairing link and phone request/reply checks over loopback.\nIncludes the remote computer module, the integrated thinking-stream UI and the Studio Git plugin UI.\nEvery installer records the same pinned qfli_git revision in BUILD_INFO.txt. Android, iOS and OHOS packages are checked for API 2 exports and the CA bundle. Desktop Git uses the installed Git CLI.\nCloud-built preview. No physical-device validation.\nAndroid uses a debug certificate. Windows is unsigned. macOS is ad-hoc signed and not notarized.\niOS and OHOS packages require signing before installation.\nThe Windows x64 remote assistant includes Node.js and agent dependencies. Extract its ZIP and open Start-QFLI-Remote.cmd.\nOn the assistant Pairing page, read the relay address and short code. In Studio, open Tools > Remote Computer > Enter short code, enter both values, and connect. Camera scanning is not implemented.\n\nWorkflow: https://github.com/azurekiln2333/qflistudio-next/actions/runs/44851658777\n"
}